A||N||8||FieroJoe||"Floating Ground" at its best...||||6||
Z||000000||FieroJoe||03-15-2001||10:43 PM||||Well, just thought I would share how messed up our GM floating ground electrical system can be.<P>This was my first electrical gremlin problem with this.  most of the time, a fuse blows and causes some totally unrelated circuit to activate, for those of you who dont know what I am talking about.<P>Anyways, I am messing around with my alarm tonight, and I took off the old siren.  The siren shares a ground with my foglamps and the relay circuit that drives it. (I use a rear defogger window switch to turn on and off the foglights)<P>So, I do some other electrical stuff, and want to make sure that the foglamp circuit still works.  I push the button, a bunch of funny relay chatter sounds, and the chime box starts going nuts!  "Whoa! I must have done something really queer!"  I though.<P>So, I checked all the connections, yep they are good, and tried it again, and same thing.  The only way to get the chime box to stop going crazy is to disconnect the battery.  I then noticed the ground for the circuit being disconnected, so I reconnect it and all is well.<P>This has been one of the wierdest electrical gremlins that I have ever had.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||6
Z||000001||Cooter||03-16-2001||12:14 AM||||My Honda Civic developed a gremlin like that while coming back from St. Augestine Florida to home above Birmingham. The car would run as long as the A/C compressor was engaged, but then the compressor would cycle off, so would the engine! I finally unplugged the A/C clutch and it ran fine all the way home- in 100+ temps with none functioning a/c. That was the vacation from hell. Turned out to be a loose ground beside the tail light panel that controlled the fuel pump. It could only get a ground by the loop created from the a/c engage circuit. That was 5 years ago, and since then I have never had anything like that happen||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||03-16-2001||03:43 AM||||not exactly elec gremlins, but you ought to try the autobody business for wierd stuff. Get all kinds of questions from parts guys that dont seem to relate. Tell them you need a front bumper and they ask if its a 4 door or has power locks and windows?? Another one I needed a tailight and they needed to know if it had elec power mirrors. I dont know, these seem pretty dumb but apparently there are differences that you wouldnt expect.||||reg||1
Z||000003||TheFiero64||03-18-2001||09:07 AM||||I had a friend that had a Dodge Shadow that needed my help. The car would run fine until someone would sit in it. The car would be running and the second you would get in all the dash warning lights would flash & the electrical stuff would go nuts. Come to find out the ground wire that ran to the chassis was broke. I guess that when you sat or pushed down on the car the little ground that was going through the motor mounts was broken and made the car shut off.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||03-18-2001||06:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TheFiero64:<BR><B>I had a friend that had a Dodge Shadow that needed my help. The car would run fine until someone would sit in it. The car would be running and the second you would get in all the dash warning lights would flash & the electrical stuff would go nuts. Come to find out the ground wire that ran to the chassis was broke. I guess that when you sat or pushed down on the car the little ground that was going through the motor mounts was broken and made the car shut off.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Wow, that is pretty crazy.  Lucky it was an easy fix though.  I bet that would be the wierdest thing in the world to have the car go nutty when you sat in it!<P><P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||MrPBody||03-18-2001||06:50 PM||||Then there was the Jag E-type that engaged its starter and lurched into my toolbox with no human assistance.  Starter relay full of water.<BR>||||reg||1
